# TODO

## General

- Consider using a centralized logging solution like ELK or Datadog or loki with Grafana for better observability.
- Cookies preferences? Terms and conditions / privacy policy / EULA?

## Security

- Add refresh replay / refresh reuse detection to the session refresh flow.
- Add edge rate limiting at the host Nginx / Cloudflare layer for authentication-sensitive endpoints.
- Secure the inference process by implementing stronger rate limiting and abuse controls.
- Secure the agents from prompt injection by implementing input filtering / guardrails before requests reach the agents.
- Continue reducing the upload DoS surface: revisit final body limits, keep attachment size/count enforcement aligned between UI and backend, and avoid large base64 payload persistence where possible.
- Add explicit size limits for persisted payload fields such as large message content & blobs.
- Harden containers further: add CPU / memory limits per service; add `read_only: true` + `tmpfs` mounts once filesystem access requirements per service are fully mapped (agents needs writable paths for deep agent file access).

## New Features

- Projects / Workspaces: group related conversations, files, agents, tools, preferences, and instructions into persistent workspaces for long-running work.
- Project-scoped memory: remember useful preferences, decisions, terminology, and context inside a specific project without mixing it into unrelated work.
- Deep Research mode: run longer multi-step research workflows with source citations, confidence notes, step traces, and exportable reports.
- Scheduled Tasks: let users create one-off or recurring agent jobs that run later, complete while the user is offline, and notify them with results.
- Artifacts / Canvas: add an editable side workspace for generated reports, markdown docs, code, tables, diagrams, JSON configs, and other reusable outputs.
- Agent run timeline: make planning, retrieval, tool calls, verification, and final-answer steps visible as a polished timeline for each agent run. Use this for the approval of a [HITL Event](https://ai-sdk.dev/elements/components/confirmation) or create a custom one. This can be used for the agentic chat stream feel as [actions](https://elements.ai-sdk.dev/components/task) or [this one](https://elements.ai-sdk.dev/components/tool).
- Voice mode: UI entrypoint done (RiVoiceprintLine icon on empty input → "coming soon" toast). Full implementation requires real-time audio streaming in UI and backend.
- Implement a long-term memory service that keep memories from all agents (e.g., episodic, procedural).
- Check how to make the streaming detached from the concept of api calls so we can like change tab and the streaming should continue for that message of the conversation like how the ai companies are doing it. if l change page or conversation the streaming should continue for that message and not get interrupted. This will require some changes in the frontend to decouple the streaming from the current conversation view and make it more global.

## Agents

- Update the retrieval process and the whole RAG pipelines so that it will be like an mcp tool calling.
- Add end-to-end non-image attachment support in inference, including deep-agent passthrough and LangGraph input normalization/parsing for file parts.

## RAG Service

- Instead of a ChromaDB consider adding pgvector in the database and use it for the retrieval, this will reduce the complexity of the system and the number of components to maintain. Also it will provide an easier way to keep the data consistent and avoid issues with synchronization between the database and the vector store.
